mainmenu "Atlas upstream host tests (built from tapeout-chipyard)"

config ATLAS_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_S
	int "Watchdog: seconds of wall time before the test is declared hung"
	default 120
	help
	  Upstream polls the Atlas status register up to 200 million times and
	  then reports a failure; on a slow link that is minutes, and some
	  tests have no timeout at all. The shim runs the test's main() in the
	  main thread and a watchdog thread that, after this many seconds,
	  writes execControl=0 (stops Atlas), prints "ATLASUP <test> TIMEOUT"
	  and ends the run with exit code 124.

	  Cannot help if a bus access itself never returns (the whole core is
	  stuck); then the last line printed before the hang names the stage.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
